Problem Statement:
	An IoT-based Smart Kitchen system can help by automating tasks, sending alerts, and monitoring kitchen conditions in real-time. This will make cooking more efficient, safer, and smarter.
	
Measuring Parameters:
	To evaluate and monitor the kitchen's performance and safety, the following parameters can be measured using sensors:
1. Temperature	
	- Prevent overcooking or overheating of appliances
	- Temperature Sensor (e.g., LM35, DHT22) - range is 0°C to 50°C
2. Humidity
	- Monitor kitchen environment (useful for storage areas)
	- Humidity Sensor (e.g., DHT22) - range is 20% to 90% RH
3. Gas Leakage (LPG/CO)	
	- Detect gas leaks for safety
	- Gas Sensor (e.g., MQ-2, MQ-6) - range is 200-10,000 ppm
4. Smoke Detection
	- Identify possible fire or burning food
	- Smoke Sensor (e.g., MQ-2) - range is 200-10,000 ppm
	
- Above 4 sensors are installed seperately and sends their data individually.
- create database and table to manage all data together along with date and time.
- create python server which will receive data from temperature and humidity sensors and store into database.
- In same python server provide REST api to get readings of all sensors and readings of given sensor.
- create python subscriber which will receive data from gas and smoke sensors and store into database.
- use thunder client to send temperature and humidity.
- use mosquito_pub to send gas and smoke reading.


Marking scheme 
Database creation and queries - 10 marks
Python Flask server - 15 marks (5 for each api)
Python subscriber - 10 marks 
REST and MQTT clients - 5 marks
	

